# PHP

Target supported PHP versions (8.2+) with strict typing and clear boundaries.

## Required behavior

- Use `declare(strict_types=1);` in new PHP files.
- Prefer typed properties, parameters, return types, and honest nullability.
- Prefer exceptions for hard failures; avoid error-suppression `@` to “make it work.”
- Use `password_hash` / `password_verify` (or framework auth hashers) for passwords — never reversible encoding.
- Treat request input as untrusted until validated/marshaled.
- Avoid dangerous APIs: `eval`, `create_function`, `unserialize` on untrusted data, shell execution of user input.
- Keep Composer autoload PSR-4 honest; do not dump class files in random roots.

## Anti-patterns

- Mixing Laravel Eloquent / Artisan mental models into PHP application code
- Untyped public APIs in new code
- `@` error suppression as control flow
- `unserialize` / `eval` on user-controlled strings
